A CELL READS AS AN INLINE RUN. The host parses each cell with `parseInlineRun` and ends it on the
next pipe, so every inline construct the host knows stands inside one.

|!Construct |!Inside a cell |h
|wikilink |[[Target]] |
|piped link |[[Label|Target]] |
|external link |[ext[caption|https://example.com]] |
|image |[img[alt text|pic.png]] |
|transclusion |{{A/Tiddler}} |
|field transclusion |{{A/Tiddler!!field}} |
|index transclusion |{{A/Tiddler##index}} |
|templated transclusion |{{A/Tiddler||A/Template}} |
|filtered transclusion |{{{ [tag[Done]sort[title]] }}} |
|macro call |<<greeting name="world">> |
|procedure call |<<my.proc a:"1" b:[[two]]>> |
|variable |<<currentTiddler>> |
|multi-valued variable |((aVariable)) |
|widget |<$link to="Target">go</$link> |
|self-closing widget |<$list filter="[tag[x]]" variable="i"/> |
|substituted attribute |<$text text=`a $(v)$ b`/> |
|html element |<span class="c">text</span> |
|conditional |<% if [[x]] %>yes<% else %>no<% endif %> |
|style run |@@color:red;styled@@ |
|class run |@@.a-class styled@@ |
|emphasis |''bold'' //italic// __under__ ~~strike~~ |
|raised and lowered |^^super^^ and ,,sub,, |
|code span |`code` |
|entities |&amp; and &#x263A; |
|comment |<!-- a note --> |

A PIPE INSIDE A CONSTRUCT BELONGS TO THE CONSTRUCT. Each pipe below stands where the host has
already entered a rule, so it ends no cell.

|attribute value |<$link to="a|b">a pipe in a value</$link> |
|call parameter |<<m "a|b">> |
|bold run |''a | b'' |
|template only |{{||A/Template}} |

EVERY ROW FORM AT ONCE. The caption stands last and the host moves it to the front, the class rows
accumulate, and each change of row type opens a container of its own.

|tbl-a tbl-b |k
|!Name |!Value |h
|one |1 |
|two |2 |
|Totals |3 |f
|tbl-c |k
|a caption carrying ''bold'' and [[a link|Target]] |c

A GRID OF SPANS. A cell holding only `>` joins the next cell, only `<` joins the cell before it, and
only `~` joins the cell above.

|!A |!B |!C |h
|a1 |>|bc1 |
|a2 |b2 |<|
|~|b3 |c3 |
|a4 |~|c4 |

VERTICAL ALIGNMENT, THEN SPACES, THEN THE HEADING MARK. The host reads a cell's leading marks in
that order, so a heading can carry both alignments.

|^ !top heading |, !bottom heading | !centred heading |h
|^top | centred | right-aligned|

A CAPTION ROW REPLACES THE ONE ABOVE IT, and a row type the table already opened opens a second
container when it returns.

|a caption the next row replaces |c
|the caption that stands |c
|!first head |h
|body |
|!second head |h
|body |
